1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:03,320
So to underscore the conflict of interest, I'm

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:05,480
going to share a very quick case study.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,520
And by the way, the resources of this

4
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:11,840
session are available along with this video.

5
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:15,140
So the case facts are those.

6
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:19,720
Grenda PLC, manufacturers of baby cereal, recently recalled

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:23,100
a batch of contaminated cereal that had reportedly

8
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:27,200
caused significant harm, including hearing and visual impairment

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,800
to many babies.

10
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:32,420
A class action has been instituted and the

11
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:36,700
board has convened an emergency meeting to decide

12
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:37,500
next steps.

13
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:40,280
A decision needs to be taken regarding legal

14
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,080
representation.

15
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,900
Across the country, there are two top law

16
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:46,260
firms with the expertise in this area of

17
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:49,760
the law, Clarkson LLP and Lakeshore LLP.

18
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,480
Clarkson has been retained by the plaintiffs.

19
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:57,280
The principal partner of Lakeshore is married to

20
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,160
the CEO of Grenda PLC.

21
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:01,180
What are the issues here?

22
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,400
The issues here are essentially around conflict of

23
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:05,880
interest.

24
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:10,180
The CEO of Grenda PLC, the manufacturers of

25
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:16,200
the contaminated baby product, is married to the

26
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:18,860
principal partner in the law firm of Clarkson

27
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:19,440
LLP.

28
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:22,060
This already suggests that there's a conflict of

29
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:22,560
interest.

30
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:26,840
In determining whether or not to proceed with

31
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:29,840
Clarkson LLP, the major consideration of the board

32
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:32,580
would be what is the best interest of

33
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:33,120
the company.

34
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:35,680
However, there are certain steps that are required

35
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,280
to be taken by the CEO of Grenda

36
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:37,740
PLC.

37
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:40,540
The first is disclosure of the conflict.

38
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:43,120
She has to disclose to the board that

39
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:47,200
her spouse is the principal partner at Clarkson

40
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:47,840
LLP.

41
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,800
After the disclosure, she has to recuse herself

42
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,420
and this means actually leaving the meeting.

43
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:56,960
If it's a virtual meeting, she needs to

44
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:57,800
exit the meeting.

45
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:00,200
If it's an in-person meeting, she needs

46
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:02,480
to also physically exit the meeting.

47
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:06,120
The remaining members of the board then have

48
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:08,400
to take a decision as to whether or

49
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:12,840
not the conflict of interest is material, whether

50
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:15,540
or not they want to go ahead with

51
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:18,760
hiring the law firm that is a related

52
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:19,300
party.

53
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:22,480
The major consideration, like I said, is what

54
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:24,780
is in the best interest of the business.

55
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,880
The best interest of the business at this

56
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,400
point is to hire the top rated law

57
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,260
firm that will be able to hold its

58
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:35,520
own against the Lakeshore that has been hired

59
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:38,320
by the plaintiffs.

60
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:41,120
And so the board will consider the best

61
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,960
interest of the company and take a decision

62
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:46,140
to hire that top rated law firm regardless

63
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,160
of the conflict of interest.

64
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:53,560
However, in communicating the information to the CEO

65
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:56,360
and in entering into the agreement with her

66
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,900
spouse, the CEO will have to refuse from

67
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,320
the engagement itself.

68
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:03,960
She's not going to be involved in the

69
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,420
negotiation of the fees.

70
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:07,700
She's not going to be involved in the

71
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:11,120
feedback from the client, from the solicitors firm,

72
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:13,840
just so that there's that separation.

73
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,060
And like I said, she'll be ring-fenced.

74
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,120
The board might even decide to set up

75
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:22,220
a board committee that would pursue the engagement

76
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:25,060
and, like I said, ring-fence the CEO.

77
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:27,140
So the steps, just to go over the

78
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:30,680
steps again, the conflict would be identified by

79
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:33,460
the director that is conflicted, whether it's a

80
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:36,480
potential conflict or one that is likely to

81
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:40,540
crystallise or one that has already manifested.

82
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:44,560
If a director is also aware that a

83
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,440
colleague on the board has a conflict of

84
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:49,560
interest, they also have a responsibility to disclose

85
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:50,280
that conflict.

86
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:53,960
So the disclosure is accepting the, identifying the

87
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:55,180
conflict is the first step.

88
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:56,880
The next step is disclosure.

89
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,040
The third step is recusal.

90
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:02,540
Recusal means exiting the meeting, not being part

91
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:06,620
of the conversation, and leaving the remaining directors

92
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:07,500
to take a decision.

93
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:13,240
And like I said, what is underlying the

94
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:15,660
decision they want to take is what is

95
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,600
in the best interest of the organisation.

96
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:21,360
The director that is conflicted is then invited

97
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:23,780
back into the room, and the board's decision

98
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:25,460
is communicated to them.

99
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:29,420
In communicating the decision to the director, there's

100
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:32,160
no need to go into the conversation that

101
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,760
had taken place because the whole essence of

102
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:36,060
having them excuse themselves in the first place

103
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:38,480
is to give the board an opportunity of

104
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:42,760
discussion without their influence or their contribution.
